  "policy": {
    "mode": "adaptive",
    "owner_date": "2026-09-20",
    "pace": {
      "ahead_gt": 15,
      "behind_lt": -10,
      "cycle_hours": 168
    },
    "bands": {
      "ok": "eligible>=3",
      "low": "eligible==2",
      "critical": "eligible==1",
      "exhausted": "eligible==0"
    },
    "admit": {
      "ok_on_pace": "all classes in the pool ranking",
      "ahead": "all classes plus the next class down",
      "behind_or_low": "judgment classes only (plan, review, verify)",
      "critical": "nothing new",
      "exhausted": "nothing"
    },
    "judgment_classes": [
      "plan",
      "review",
      "verify",
      "design",
      "audit"
    ],
    "source_of_truth": "~/.agents/policy/coding-agents/ROUTING.md",
    "lineup": {
      "owner_date": "2026-09-22",
      "drivers": [
        "opus-latest",
        "sol-latest"
      ],
      "retired": "see top-level `retired`: Fable, the whole Astra family, the gpt-5.6 generation and older",
      "implementation": "~/.claude/rules/models.md is the local source (2026-09-25): Opus plans, specs, designs and verifies; implement goes gpt-implementer (sol-latest, medium) > sonnet-implementer > opus-latest (pace-gated); mechanical goes luna-implementer (luna-latest, medium) > cursor-seat (grok-latest) > devin-seat (swe-latest)."
    }
  },
  "notes": [
    "Codex seats take --model <id> plus a separate --effort; the effort suffix is not a model name.",
    "2026-09-22 canonical lineup (owner): no Fable, no Codex Astra, no gpt-5.6. Seats name family aliases (`aliases`); `route resolve <alias>` and `route pick` resolve them to the newest served, non-retired model, so a release needs no edit. Opus orchestrates; cheaper seats implement; the other vendor's stronger model audits (classes.*.audit).",
    "2026-09-22: glm-*/kimi-* chain entries removed: cursor-agent serves neither (cursor-agent --list-models) and no other seat dispatches them, so they could only ever resolve to a literal wildcard. Re-add them behind a family alias once a seat can run GLM or Kimi.",
    "2026-09-25: Cursor and Devin accounts are registered in agent-lb (`seat accounts`, ~/.agent-lb/seats). cursor-seat and devin-seat dispatch through `seat run`, which picks an account, fails over on a limit or auth error and writes the receipt; /api/pools serves `cursor` and `devin` as cli_seat pools from the seat state. Neither vendor offers a supported API for subscription models, so there is no request-level route through the LB.",
    "2026-09-25: the `implementer` seat (a Sonnet forwarder to Codex terra-latest) is retired. terra-latest is unserved (gpt-6-terra is not in the upstream catalog, gpt-5.6-terra is retired) and no seat uses it. Implementation runs on the ccgpt-bridge seats gpt-implementer and luna-implementer, local unmanaged definitions in ~/.claude/agents."
  ],
